     "text": "The basilar artery also sends branches to the cerebellum, which controls balance and helps coordinate movement.",
     "defines": "cerebellum",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "quote": "The basilar artery is an anastomosis that begins at the junction of the two vertebral arteries and sends branches to the cerebellum and brain stem.",
       "section": "20.5 Circulatory Pathways",
       "url": "https://openstax.org/books/anatomy-and-physiology-2e/pages/20-5-circulatory-pathways",
